# Pinch — Cursor Agent Rules

## Who I am
A design-forward software engineer who values precision over speed.
Briefly explain tradeoffs when making architectural decisions to help me 
understand the why before implementing.

## Behavior
- Do not be sycophantic. Critique my ideas when necessary.
- If you see a flaw in my approach, say so directly before implementing.
- Ask ONE clarifying question if genuinely uncertain. Do not assume.
- State your plan in plain English before writing any code.
- Prefer the smallest change that solves the problem. Do not refactor 
  unrelated code while fixing something specific.
- If a better pattern exists for what I'm asking, name it and ask 
  before proceeding.

## Stack
- Angular 17+ standalone components
- Firebase/Firestore via RecipeFirestoreService — never bypass this service
- Tailwind CSS only — no inline styles, no external CSS files
- Angular Reactive Forms with FormBuilder
- TypeScript strict mode — no `any`, no implicit nulls, explicit return
  types on all functions

## Architecture rules
- Enforce the Facade pattern — components talk to Facades, never
  directly to infrastructure services
- Do not create new services without asking first
- Do not touch auth logic unless explicitly asked
- Reuse existing patterns before creating new abstractions
- If you see a TODO comment, flag it but do not resolve it unless asked

## Maintainability
- Extract repeated logic into private methods, not inline blocks
- Keep component methods under ~20 lines — if longer, suggest extraction
- Name booleans as questions: `isLoading`, `hasError`, `isDemo`
- One responsibility per method — a method that fetches AND transforms
  data should be split
- Use JSDoc syntax for all public-facing method doc blocks

## Performance
- Avoid subscribing inside loops or ngFor — flag it if you see it
- Use `trackBy` on all `*ngFor` directives
- Prefer `OnPush` change detection — flag components that could use it
- Use the async pipe in templates to manage subscriptions
- Do not add new npm packages without asking

## Forms
- All forms use FormBuilder with nonNullable controls unless
  null is semantically meaningful
- Clear related controls explicitly via valueChanges when
  dependencies change (e.g. customUnit when unit !== 'custom')

## Mobile-first
- All new UI components must be reviewed for mobile layout first
- Touch targets minimum 44px
- No hover-only interactions — always provide tap equivalent

## Git
- Never use `git add .` or `git add -A`
- Stage files explicitly: `git add <file_path>` or `git add -p`
- Before staging, explain which files were modified and why they
  belong together
- Atomic commits — smallest possible change per functional unit
- No unrelated changes in one commit
- Conventional commits format: `<type>(scope): <description>`
  e.g. `feat(ui): add navbar` — imperative mood, lowercase